Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Pipe shells: a caller can ask for corners from a smaller turn of the
spine's tangent between two of its edges than 1e-2 rad (mitcad#1559):
BRepOffsetAPI_MakePipeShell::SetTransitionMode(Mode, theAngleMin).
MitCad's pipes ask for mitred corners from 1e-4 rad on.

BRepOffsetAPI_MakePipeShell::SetTransitionMode sets BRepFill_PipeShell's
transition with its default angles. Under Angmin, two edges' laws are
joined by turning the second's whole frame onto the first's end frame
(BRepFill_LocationLaw::TransformInCompatibleLaw), so through a kink of up
to 1e-2 rad (0.57 degrees) the section kept the first edge's frame and
leaned from square by the kink all along the second edge: 0.05 and 0.3
degrees along two B-spline pieces meeting at those angles. With 1e-4 rad
(0.0057 degrees) for mitred corners (BRepBuilderAPI_RightCorner) such a
kink is a corner, and the section is square to each edge.
Joints of pieces meant to be tangent, whose tangents differ by the noise
of their approximation (an intersection curve's pieces of chains joined
tangentially: some 2e-6 rad), stay under it.

Rounded corners keep 1e-2 rad: the turn of a section about a slight kink
is a sliver that does not close (a closed stirrup of lines and arcs whose
arcs meet two lines at 0.12 degrees came out invalid with rounded corners
there, where a pipe's mitre elsewhere had failed).

The first versions changed the default (of SetTransition, then of
SetTransitionMode for mitred corners). Every pipe got corners at slight
kinks then, among them OCCT's sweeps along splines divided at their
approximation's kinks of 0.02 to 0.2 degrees (bugs/modalg_7 bug32445,
whose result became invalid, and bug32447_1, whose faces changed): the
mode alone keeps OCCT's angles since mitcad#1899.

Test: geometry/tests/test_pipe_square_section.cpp (ctest
geometry.pipe_square_section): test_four_lines and test_kink (with 1661),
and test_stirrup, whose kink of 0.12 degrees is a mitred corner since this
patch: a valid solid within 0.2 % of the circle's area times the path's
length. It fails without the patch: the test does not build without it
(shown 2026-11-20 by tools/occt-port-proof.py).

